\section{Ethical Business Practices}

\subsection{Anti-Corruption Framework}

The Company maintains a comprehensive anti-corruption framework aligned with international best practices and Indonesian regulatory requirements. Our anti-corruption policy explicitly prohibits all forms of bribery, extortion, and corrupt practices in both public and private sectors. The policy applies to all employees, directors, contractors, and business partners operating within the Company's value chain.

The framework incorporates risk-based due diligence procedures for third-party relationships, with enhanced scrutiny applied to high-risk jurisdictions and sectors. All employees receive mandatory anti-corruption training, with specialized modules for procurement, sales, and government relations functions. The Company maintains a confidential reporting mechanism for suspected violations, with protections against retaliation for whistleblowers.

\subsection{Compliance with Indonesian Anti-Corruption Laws}

Our anti-corruption program is designed to ensure full compliance with Indonesia's Anti-Corruption Law (UU No. 31/1999 jo UU No. 20/2001) and related regulations. The Company has established internal controls that exceed statutory requirements, including mandatory disclosure of conflicts of interest, restrictions on gifts and hospitality, and regular audits of high-risk transactions.

The Board of Directors reviews anti-corruption compliance annually, with findings reported to the Audit Committee. The Company participates in industry associations that promote anti-corruption best practices and engages with law enforcement agencies to support investigations when appropriate.

\subsection{Whistleblower Protection Mechanisms}

The Company has implemented a robust whistleblower protection program that provides multiple reporting channels, including a dedicated hotline, email address, and in-person reporting options. All reports are investigated by an independent compliance team, with findings escalated to senior management and the Board as appropriate.

Protection measures include confidentiality of the reporter's identity, protection from retaliation, and support throughout the investigation process. The program has successfully identified and addressed several potential violations, demonstrating its effectiveness in promoting ethical behavior.

\subsection{Supply Chain Ethics}

The Company extends its ethical standards to suppliers and contractors through a comprehensive supplier code of conduct. All new suppliers must complete due diligence questionnaires and certify compliance with anti-corruption requirements. The Company conducts regular audits of high-risk suppliers and maintains the right to terminate relationships with non-compliant parties.

Training programs for suppliers include modules on anti-corruption compliance, with certification required for continued business relationships. The Company shares best practices and resources to help suppliers improve their compliance programs, recognizing that ethical supply chains benefit all stakeholders.

\subsection{Ethical Decision-Making Framework}

The Company has established an ethical decision-making framework that guides employees in navigating complex situations. This framework incorporates stakeholder considerations, legal requirements, and corporate values to ensure consistent application of ethical principles across all business decisions.

Regular case studies and scenario-based training help employees develop practical skills in ethical decision-making. The framework is reviewed annually to ensure it remains relevant to emerging challenges and evolving stakeholder expectations.

\subsection{Monitoring and Enforcement}

The Company maintains a comprehensive monitoring program that includes regular audits, transaction reviews, and compliance assessments. Violations of anti-corruption policies are subject to disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment or contract termination.

The compliance team produces quarterly reports to the Board on the effectiveness of anti-corruption controls and emerging risks. The Company also participates in external assurance reviews to validate the effectiveness of its anti-corruption program.

\subsection{Continuous Improvement}

The Company regularly reviews and updates its anti-corruption framework to address emerging risks and incorporate lessons learned from investigations and industry developments. Recent enhancements include expanded due diligence requirements for digital transactions and enhanced controls for remote work arrangements.

The Company actively participates in industry working groups focused on anti-corruption best practices and contributes to the development of sector-specific guidance. These collaborative efforts help advance anti-corruption efforts across the broader business community.

\subsection{Stakeholder Engagement}

The Company engages with various stakeholders to promote ethical business practices and gather feedback on our anti-corruption program. This engagement includes regular dialogue with civil society organizations, participation in multi-stakeholder initiatives, and transparent reporting on anti-corruption efforts.

The Company responds to stakeholder concerns and incorporates feedback into program improvements. This collaborative approach helps build trust and demonstrates our commitment to ethical business practices.

\subsection{Performance Metrics}

The Company tracks key performance indicators to measure the effectiveness of its anti-corruption program, including:
- Number of reported concerns and their resolution rates
- Results of compliance audits and assessments
- Training completion rates and effectiveness scores
- Third-party due diligence completion rates
- Incidents of non-compliance and their severity

These metrics are reviewed quarterly by the Board and used to drive continuous improvement in our anti-corruption efforts.

