As Indonesia's state-owned energy company, Pertamina has made significant strides in transitioning towards sustainable energy solutions. The company has invested USD 2.5 billion in renewable energy projects, including geothermal, solar, and biofuel initiatives \cite{{Pertamina_RenewableEnergy2023}}.

Pertamina's environmental initiatives include a comprehensive methane emission reduction program that has achieved a 15\% reduction in methane emissions from its operations since 2020 \cite{{Pertamina_MethaneReduction2022}}. The company has also committed to achieving net-zero emissions in its operations by 2060, with interim targets of 30\% reduction by 2030 \cite{{Pertamina_NetZero2023}}.

