Indofood CBP has demonstrated leadership in sustainable agriculture and food security, with its "Sustainable Agriculture" program covering over 100,000 hectares of farmland \cite{{Indofood_SustainableAgriculture2023}}. The company has implemented water-efficient irrigation systems that have reduced water consumption by 25\% in its agricultural operations \cite{{Indofood_WaterEfficiency2022}}.

The company's social initiatives include the "NutriPlan" program, which has provided nutritional support to over 500,000 children in underserved communities \cite{{Indofood_NutriPlan2023}}. Indofood has also committed to achieving 100\% sustainable sourcing of its key agricultural commodities by 2025 \cite{{Indofood_SustainableSourcing2023}}.

\subsection{PT XL Axiata Tbk}

XL Axiata has integrated ESG principles across its telecommunications operations, with a particular focus on digital inclusion and environmental sustainability. The company's "XL Future Leaders" program has trained over 10,000 young Indonesians in digital skills and leadership \cite{{XL_SustainabilityReport2023}}.

XL Axiata's environmental initiatives include a comprehensive energy efficiency program that has reduced energy consumption by 20\% across its network infrastructure \cite{{XL_EnergyEfficiency2022}}. The company has also implemented a circular economy approach to e-waste management, with over 95\% of its electronic waste being recycled or reused \cite{{XL_EWasteManagement2023}}.

These leading ESG performers demonstrate that sustainable business practices can drive both environmental and social impact while maintaining strong financial performance. Their initiatives provide valuable models for other Indonesian companies seeking to enhance their ESG performance and contribute to the country's sustainable development goals.

